  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the largest federal contracts by total value for FY2026 to date. HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC tops the list with $51.3B in total contract value. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP follows with $48.1B, and NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC holds $42.8B. The list includes government contractors and federally funded research organizations with large, multi-year contract portfolios: UT-BATTELLE LLC at $42.3B, LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $41.3B, and REGENTS OF THE UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA, THE at $35.3B. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION each appear with $35.1B. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is listed at $34.9B, and CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC is listed at $34.4B. The dataset reports total award values as full contract values, not single-year obligations. Total obligations reported on the page equal $51.3B. This snapshot highlights which entities hold the largest contract portfolios by total value in FY2026 to date.",
